+### `removeWhere(predicate)` -> `int`
+
+Remove every item for which `predicate(value, index)` returns a truthy value.
+The predicate receives values in logical front-to-back order and the original
+zero-based index of each value. Remaining values retain their order. The
+predicate must be a function; an error is thrown otherwise. If the predicate
+throws, the queue is unchanged.
+
+Returns the number of removed items.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1,2,3,4]);
+denque.removeWhere(function (value) { return value % 2 === 0; }); // 2
+denque.toArray(); // [1,3]
+```
+
+
+
 ### `splice(int index, int count, item1, item2, ...)` -> `array`
 
 Native splice implementation.
